  "body": "What changed:\r\n- `engage_level` ramps the wall side (new `contour_wall_ramp.rs`) when the entry is ramp or helix.\r\n  The zig-zag runs along the lead-in and the ring, with the same helper as the bore side.\r\n- A helix stands down to the same ramp and says so once.\r\n- A tabbed level, or a path too short for the angle, still grazes and says why.\r\n- The test `a_wall_side_entry_is_refused_by_name_grazing_unchanged` pinned the old refusal. It\r\n  is replaced by three tests. `an_entry_edit_marks_the_contour_stale_and_the_wall_regen_ramps`\r\n  (app) changes with it.\r\n\r\nReadings (Ø10 tool, 30 x 30 part, 3 levels, 5 degrees): worst descent 5.00 degrees, no axial\r\ndive, no plunge move. Every cutter-centre point stays one tool radius off the part.\r\n\r\nPinning tests (`camcraft-motion`, `machining2d`): `a_wall_side_ramp_entry_ramps_every_level_within_its_angle`,\r\n`a_wall_side_helix_stands_down_to_the_same_ramp_and_says_so_once`,\r\n`a_wall_side_ramp_too_short_for_its_angle_grazes_and_says_why`.\r\n\r\nBehaviour change: a file that stored entry ramp or helix on an outside contour now posts a\r\nramp where it posted a graze. The default (plunge) is unchanged.\r\n\r\nNot exercised:\r\n- A real part with tabs and a non-rectangular outline.\r\n- The Mach4 post and the heavy lanes.\r\n- Outside contours with several rings: the later rings still plunge through the pass link\r\n  (issue #3829 does not cover that; it needs its own issue).\r\n\r\nQuick gate (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate quick`, Windows, `core.autocrlf=true`, 1183 steps): the run stopped at step 1157 of 1183 (session end); all steps up to there were ok except `sinumerik_810m_post`. The UI steps were rerun apart: `catalog_render`, `egui_app`, `trace_composite`, `trace_parity` red (exit 101), the rest ok. clippy green.\r\nBaseline: the same steps on unmodified `origin/main` (run by name):\r\n- `sinumerik_810m_post`, `catalog_render` and `egui_app` are red on main too. The first two read a\r\n  golden or example file that the CRLF checkout changed. `egui_app` exits 101 on main.\r\n- `trace_composite` and `trace_parity` crash with an access violation on both main and the\r\n  branch, on some runs and not on others (main: 3 of 3 manual runs crashed, 2 gate runs passed).\r\n- `clippy -D warnings` is green on main and on this branch.\r\nNo red step is new on this branch.\r\n\r\nChangelog: An outside 2D Contour with entry ramp or helix ramps onto each level along the lead-in and the ring.\r\n\r\nFixes #3829\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
